---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { lastUpdated, lastUpdatedHuman } from '../data/now';
import { PERSON_ID } from '../data/person';
import { currentBooks, magazines, podcasts, regularAuthor, currentMusic } from '../data/reading';

const title = 'Adrian Watkins | What I’m Working on Now';
const description = 'Adrian Watkins’s current work, reading and interests: commercial leadership, data protection, democratising.ai and mentoring, from his home in Singapore.';
const nowJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'What Adrian Watkins is working on now', url: 'https://adrianwatkins.com/now',
  description, dateModified: lastUpdated, about: { '@id': PERSON_ID },
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} current="now" jsonLd={nowJsonLd}>
  <section class="stub" style="padding-bottom:32px">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow">/now</div>
      <h1>What I’m working on, right now.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Work, ideas and the things holding my attention. Based in Singapore, updated when something meaningful changes.</p>
      <p class="quiet" style="font-size:13px;margin-top:8px">Last updated: <time datetime={lastUpdated}>{lastUpdatedHuman}</time>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container now-grid">
  <section class="now-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow">01 / In practice</div><h2>Leading.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>I lead commercial operations and governance across <a href="https://sqreem.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SQREEM Technologies</a>, working across markets to connect strategy with everyday execution.</p>
        <p>My recently formalised responsibilities as the Data Protection Officer (DPO) build on work I have been doing over the past year. Right now, I’m spending considerable time with official papers and decisions on data privacy across the EU, US and Australia, understanding what they mean for product, commercial and operational decisions across jurisdictions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="now-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow">02 / In the making</div><h2>Building.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>I’m continuing to improve DARE, the shared publishing and data platform behind <a href="https://democratising.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">democratising.ai</a>, along with the publications, data services and tools it supports.</p>
        <p>A particular focus is taking <a href="https://urbandogowner.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Urban Dog Owner</a> further: making it more useful for people navigating life with a dog in Singapore, from adoption and everyday care to discovering places together, and helping local businesses connect with customers who will appreciate what they offer.</p>
        <p>I’m also refining how I explain <a href="/edge">EDGE</a> and help people put it into practice. The framework brings structure to business thinking and decisions, with AI-powered tools supporting exploration, preparation and reflection.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="now-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow">03 / Giving back</div><h2>Contributing.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>I’m exploring how I can do more for students in Singapore. I joined the in-person mentoring session at the Social Impact Catalyst edition of <a href="https://www.ggef.com/sdgopenhack" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SDG Open Hack</a> on 12 September. My next confirmed session is at Nanyang Polytechnic on 23 September. These sessions are a way to contribute, learn from students and understand where my experience can be useful.</p>
        <p>I’d like to build on that through further mentoring, guest sessions and practical workshops.</p>
        <p>Alongside my Singapore commitments, I continue supporting founders across the region. I have also recently been appointed a mentor for the <a href="https://aseanfoundation.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ASEAN Foundation</a>’s ASEAN SOAR Together programme.</p>
        <p><a href="/singapore">My contribution in Singapore</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="reading" class="now-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow">04 / On my bookshelf</div><h2>Reading.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>On my current reading pile: {currentBooks.map((book, index) => (
          <Fragment>{index > 0 && ' and '}{book.affiliateUrl ? <a href={book.affiliateUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored noopener noreferrer"><em>{book.title}</em></a> : <em>{book.title}</em>} by {book.author}</Fragment>
        ))}.</p>
        {currentBooks.some(book => book.affiliateUrl) && <p class="quiet">As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases.</p>}
        <p>For current affairs and opinion, I read <a href={magazines[0].url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><em>{magazines[0].name}</em></a> and <a href={magazines[1].url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><em>{magazines[1].name}</em></a>. For chuckles, <a href={magazines[2].url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><em>{magazines[2].name}</em></a>.</p>
        <p>Alongside those, I’m neck-deep in official data privacy papers from the EU, US and Australia. Different reading, equally capable of keeping me occupied.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="now-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow">05 / On repeat</div><h2>Listening.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Regular listens include <a href={podcasts[0].url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><em>{podcasts[0].name}</em></a>, <a href={podcasts[1].url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><em>{podcasts[1].name}</em></a> and <a href={podcasts[2].url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><em>{podcasts[2].name}</em></a>, The Athletic’s Manchester United podcast.</p>
        <p>I also listen to <a href={podcasts[3].url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><em>{podcasts[3].name}</em></a> by {podcasts[3].host}.</p>
        <p>I also tend to find time for anything <a href={regularAuthor.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{regularAuthor.name}</a> publishes or appears on.</p>
        <p>Music is a big part of my life too. Right now, I’m rediscovering the full <a href={currentMusic.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><em>{currentMusic.name}</em></a> collection.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="now-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow">06 / Open questions</div><h2>Thinking about.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>How changing privacy expectations across countries and regions should shape everyday business decisions.</p>
        <p>How I can contribute more to Singapore students, and what would make Urban Dog Owner more useful to the people who rely on it.</p>
        <p>And whether leaving every Manchester United player out of my Fantasy football team makes me a bad Manchester United fan. Loyalty and judgement are occasionally in discussion.</p>
        <p><a href="/contact">Get in touch</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .now-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 48px 48px; padding-top: 32px; padding-bottom: 80px; }
  .now-section { padding: 24px 0 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line, #b8ad98); scroll-margin-top: 80px; min-width: 0; }
  .now-section > .container { width: 100%; padding: 0; max-width: none; }
  .now-section h2 { margin: 10px 0 20px; }
  .now-section .prose { max-width: none; }
  .now-section .quiet { font-size: 13px; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .now-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 36px; } }
</style>
